      "id": "nm5ch4t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Importance of Agriculture in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agriculture is the primary source of livelihood for over 50% of India's population and serves as the foundation for major agro-based industries.",
        "Agricultural activities in India are structured around three distinct cropping seasons: Kharif (monsoon), Rabi (winter), and Zaid (summer).",
        "Rice and wheat constitute the primary food staple crops of the country, with India ranking second globally in their production.",
        "The Green Revolution initiated in the mid-1960s drastically increased crop yields through High Yielding Varieties (HYV) seeds, chemical fertilizers, and controlled irrigation.",
        "Major agricultural challenges include land fragmentation, dependence on monsoons, soil degradation, and groundwater over-exploitation."
      ],
      "id": "45qg0in"
    },
